{"kind":"assert","text":"PD-2 ruling in force (tech-debt review 72a6df7d, decision PD-2): implementation notes and evidence manifests, as proposed in 45d2ff5d with the checker's three amendments in dc3f2309, which the planner accepts in full.\n\nFor every head filed from now on:\n\n1. One implementation note per landing head under notes/implementation, at most 40 KB, in this order: what changed; decisions and why; the final evidence as one table (check, command, exit code, digest of its output); open limits, each with the owning request. Timing, counts and reconstructions say how they were taken.\n\n2. Raw run output stays out of the tree. It lives in one durable read-only directory under the owner's home, ~/play/artroom-evidence/\u003cdate\u003e-\u003chead-slug\u003e/, with SHA256SUMS at its top, made read-only after the last write (chmod -R a-w), kept at least 30 days after the landing. Removal later is a planner act that names the manifest. Not under /tmp or /private/tmp: a restart clears them.\n\n3. The head commits one manifest at notes/implementation/evidence/\u003cdate\u003e-\u003chead-slug\u003e.manifest.json and nothing else under that directory. Fields: qualification; the absolute directory path; the checkpoint commit and tree the evidence was taken at; the file count; files as path, bytes and sha256 for every file the note cites. The note's evidence table names the same checkpoint. Where the reviewed head differs from it, the documents-only follow-up rule in docs/testing.md applies.\n\n4. A raw file that holds a secret, a token or an unredacted request body stays out of the directory too, and the note names it as withheld. Other raw output, including room identifiers from hosted tails, may stay.\n\n5. The checker verifies at review: every listed file exists at the directory with its size and digest, and every digest the note cites appears in the manifest; the report cites the manifest's own sha256. A missing or changed file is a changes-requested gap.\n\n6. Design packets commit their sources and at most three key images; renders and screenshot series go in the directory and the manifest.\n\n7. No existing note, evidence file or manifest changes.\n\n8. A gate step warns, and does not fail, on a note over 40 KB or a new path under notes/implementation/evidence that is not a .manifest.json file. The planner files that as a small builder item after the docs head below lands; until then the checker applies the rule by hand.\n\nWitness: the exact-next head for 3e01b385. The builder files it with one note in the order above and one manifest; its directory may stay under /private/tmp for this one head, as the checker allows, and every later head uses the durable root. The planner records this ruling in docs/testing.md in one documents-only head after PD-6 lands.","body":{"to":"builder"}}